Previously, VR[ cameras could] record a[ partial] torso of a person[, but the 8]i Portal goes beyond that. It enables “[complete freedom] of movement,” and it gives you a sense of “presence,” or the feeling that you are there in the virtual space with the person. It creates[ a] more “emotional connection with the person you are watching,” the company said in the video below.
